when the shield premiered on FX in 2002  the program pushed the limits of what  could be portrayed on cable programming  it's been well over a decade since the  series helped spark a small screen  revolution so let's look back at some  little-known facts about this  extraordinary show this is the untold  truth of the shield risky business  before 2002 the only original series on  FX was the Baywatch parody son of the  beach once the shield joined the lineup  the series broke new ground testing the  limits on violence nudity and language  it was very risky material open your  mouth baited the emmy-winning series  centered around corrupt cop Vic Mackey  masterfully played by Michael Chiklis  Mackey leads an experimental anti-gang  unit within the LAPD often using highly  unethical means to fight crime inspired  by the success of the shield the network  brought other edgy new shows into the  fold like nip/tuck damages and Rescue Me  Chiklis told TV week I think the face of  basic cable was changed forever it made  a lot of people think why can't we the  walking dead connection in 2007 Frank  Darabont the writer director of the  Shawshank Redemption took a break from  big-budget filmmaking to direct an  episode of the shield after filming the  season 6 episode chasing ghosts Darabont  wanted to further explore televisions  possibilities it wasn't long before he  started developing a zombie horror  series based on the comic book The  Walking Dead bringing The Walking Dead -  TV proved to be an uphill battle with  network execs but when AMC finally  greenlit the post-apocalyptic series  Darabont remembered his roots and  enlisted some of the shield's production  team including Charles eglee and Glen  Mazzara The Walking Dead's future  showrunner Michael Chiklis his  transformation before the shield Michael  Chiklis was known for playing much  cuddler characters like Tony Scali the  police officer in ABC's the Commish but  the actor was tired of being typecast  telling the archive of American  television that a conversation with his  wife Michelle Moran inspired him to make  a career change  she told him it's not incumbent upon the  studios and the network's to reinvent  you it's incumbent upon you to reinvent  yourself that reinvention of course  required Chiklis to also reinvent his  physique in order to land different  rolls according to Men's Journal Chiklis  relied on healthy portion controlled  meals and ran seven miles a day six days  a week to transform his appearance and I  just hit the gym three hours a day and I  got in sick shape at that time the hard  work paid off despite what Family Guy  would lead you to believe no matter how  muscular I get I will never be muscular  Walton Goggins ordeal before the shield  took TV by storm Walton Goggins was  known mainly for bid parts in 90s  programs like in the heat of the night  I've always got it man  taking on the role of Shane Vendrell put  the future star in the spotlight but  execs hated his performance early on in  fact he was almost fired from the show  he told Nashville Scene the brass at FX  saw the pilot and they thought is he  irritating I can't read him  if Goggins had never played Shane and  the shield he may have never gotten to  play memorable characters like justified  spoi Crowder or the hateful aids Chris  Mannix would anyone want to live in that  reality game over back in 2006 Fox  teamed up with Sony to release 24 the  game for the PlayStation 2 Kiefer  Sutherland fans got to step into Jack  Bauer's shoes battling bad guys against  the ticking clock a year later the  shield tried the same formula a game  based on the show was released for the  PlayStation 2 in PC much like the 24  game the shield was a third-person  shooter the game involved a gang war  between two rival crews and it wasn't  well-received at all in its two-star  review IGN said you'd be better off  avoiding this one as it makes great  strides to damage the otherwise high  quality of the franchise in other words  this experiments failed  go on arrest me a murderous reality  throughout the run of the show actor  Michael chase played the role of officer  Julian Lowe a strict Christian who hid  his homosexuality from his wife and crew  in 2014 the actors career came to a  violent halt Jayce was arrested for  fatally shooting his wife April in front  of their two sons prosecutors claimed  their horrific crime was motivated by  jealousy the mirror shared part of the  trials transcript claiming Jace admitted  he was angry at the time and said all I  intended to do was shoot her in the leg  and then I shot her in the leg and that  was it  Jace was convicted of second-degree  murder and sentenced to 40 years to life  in prison a shield reunion TV reboots  like the recently revived Will &amp; Grace  are all the rage right now so it's  understandable that fans of the shield  wonder if the show might return one day  sounds like series creator Sean Ryan is  kicking the idea around to during a  panel discussion at the 2016 SAT X  television festival he said I don't know  where Vic Mackey is until someone puts  me in a writers room so could Vic Mackey  return one day ryan tells Entertainment  Weekly I've never definitively decided  what Vic Mackey is doing now as a fan of  the shield I'm interested  seeing that so are we thanks for  watching click the looper icon to  subscribe to our youtube channel plus  check out all this cool stuff we know  you'll love to  [Music]  [Applause]
 

